Note = {Apoptosis 2008 World - From Mechanisms to Applications, Luxembourg,
   LUXEMBOURG, JAN 23-26, 2008},
Abstract = {This study was conducted to examine the neuroprotective effects of
   acetone extracts from Viola mandshurica (VME). The effect of VME on
   hydrogen peroxide (H2O2)-induced DNA damage in PC12 cells was evaluated
   by the comet assay where VME (100 and 250 mu g/mL) was a dose-dependent
   inhibitor of DNA damage induced by 500 mu mol/L of H2O2. The protective
   effect of VME against H2O2-induced oxidative damage on PC12 cells was
   investigated by an MTT {[}3-(4,5-dimethylthiazol-2-yl)-2,5-diphenyl
   tetrazolium bromide] reduction assay and lactate dehydrogenase (LDH)
   release assays. After 3 It of cell exposure to 500 mu mol/L of H2O2, a
   marked reduction in cen survival was observed. However, the reduction
   was significantly prevented by 100 and 250 mu g/mL of VME. H2O2 also
   induced severe apoptosis of the PC 12 cells, which was indicated by
   Hoechst 33342 staining. Interestingly, the H2O2-stressed PC12 cells that
   were incubated with 100 and 250 mu g/mL of VME had greatly suppressed
   apoptosis. The results suggest that VME could be a new antioxidant
   candidate against neuronal diseases.},
